<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panama Canal Authority</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1997">1997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Autoridad del Canal de Panamá</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> Authority is the autonomous Panamanian government agency that has operated the Panama Canal since 31 December 1999, when it took over from the US-run Panama Canal Commission. Created under a constitutional amendment and a law of 1997, it is run on commercial lines and pays large revenues to the national treasury. It carried out the expansion of the canal with new, larger locks, opened in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panama-canal-authority.jpg" alt="Panama Canal Authority" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Panama.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
